.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-WEBUI 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-webui
.Nd the kldload web console: install, virtual machines, clusters, storage and more, from a browser
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -unix-socket Ar path
.Op Fl -port Ar port
.Op Fl -bind Ar address
.Op Fl -no-tls
.Op Fl -no-browser
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
serves the web console's pages and the WebSocket its pages use to act on
the machine, as root: installing, making and deleting virtual machines,
building clusters, opening terminals.
On an installed machine
.Pa kldload-webui.service
runs it on a unix socket that only
.Xr nginx 8
reaches, and nginx serves it on port 8443 with the machine's certificate.
.Pp
Who may act:
.Bl -tag -width "on the live image"
.It on the live image
anyone at the console, for the install;
.It installed
a browser that has signed in.
Signing in takes a member of the administrators' group
.Pq Ql wheel No or Ql sudo
and their system password, checked by PAM, or the bearer token in
.Pa /etc/kldload/webui-token
for scripts.
Being on the same machine is not enough.
.El
.Pp
A sign-in makes a session that lasts 30 days.
The browser keeps it as a cookie the page's scripts cannot read, and
sends it with every connection, so each browser signs in once.
nginx asks
.Nm
about the same cookie before it serves the tools behind the console
(the terminals, Grafana, Headlamp, Open WebUI), so they need the same
sign-in.
A password session ends early if its user leaves the administrators'
group.
If PAM cannot be used the password is refused.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -unix-socket Ar path
Serve on this socket, for nginx.
.It Fl -port Ar port , Fl -bind Ar address
Serve on TCP instead; default port 8080 on every address.
.It Fl -no-tls
Plain HTTP, when something in front terminates TLS.
.It Fl -no-browser
Do not open a browser.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/kldload/webui-token
The bearer token, mode 0600, made on first run.
.It Pa /var/lib/kldload/webui-sessions.json
The sessions, mode 0600, as hashes of the cookie values.
Deleting it and restarting the service signs every browser out.
.It Pa /run/kldload/webui.sock
The socket.
.It Pa /usr/local/share/kldload-webui/
The pages.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
It serves until stopped.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Reading the token for a script; not run for this page:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# cat /etc/kldload/webui-token
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload-proxy 8 ,
.Xr kldload-session 8 ,
.Xr kldload-tls-cert 8 ,
.Xr nginx 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-05-21 the WebSocket was found to accept any client that reached
the port, as root; the token was added.
On 2026-09-23 letting loopback in without a password was confined to the
unix socket.
On 2026-09-30 it was removed: an installed console signs in, and the
terminals behind it moved from loopback ports to sockets only nginx can
open.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Anyone who can sign in can act as root through the console; that is
what the administrators' group is for.
A signed-in browser stays signed in for 30 days, including on a shared
desktop account.
